{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:1", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The opening word 'ulakelām' ('all the world'): the Lord whom all the world cannot know or tell, who dances in the hall, is praised.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:cekkilar"], "notes": "Tradition: the word was given by Śiva from the sky. Paraphrase of the rest of the verse moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:cantesura-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "cantesura-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "The boy Caṇṭēcurar struck his father's feet when he kicked over the milk being offered to Śiva; Śiva made him chief of his servants.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:cantesvara-nayanar"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:kannappa-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "kannappa-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "The hunter Kaṇṇappar's worship with tasted meat, water from his mouth and flowers from his hair pleased Śiva more than the priest's correct rites; when the liṅga's eye bled he gave his own eye, and was stopped by Śiva from giving the second.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:kannappar"], "notes": "Section-level locator (the purāṇam of Kaṇṇappar).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:karaikkal-ammaiyar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "karaikkal-ammaiyar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Kāraikkāl Ammaiyār asked Śiva for undying love, no rebirth — or, if reborn, never to forget him — and to sing at his feet while he dances; he granted it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:karaikkal-ammaiyar"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:pucala-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "pucala-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Pūcalār built a temple in his mind, and Śiva chose to be present first at its consecration rather than at the king's temple of stone.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:pucalar"], "practices": ["prc:manasa-puja"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:siruttonta-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "siruttonta-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Ciṟuttoṇṭar and his wife gave even their only son to feed Śiva disguised as an ascetic, and the son was restored — teaching that nothing is withheld from a devotee of Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:siruttontar"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:tirumula-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "tirumula-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "The yogī from Kailāsa entered the body of the dead herdsman Mūlaṉ out of compassion for his cows, and, his own body taken away, stayed as Tirumūlar singing the Tirumantiram.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "teachers": ["tch:tirumular"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:tirunalaippovar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "tirunalaippovar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Nantaṉār, an outcaste, was admitted to Śiva's presence at Chidambaram after passing through fire at the Lord's command and rising as a sage.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:nantanar"], "disputes": ["dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "notes": "Section-level locator.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:tirunanacampantar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "tirunanacampantar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Campantar, fed with the milk of knowledge by Umā at three, sang Śiva's hymns throughout the Tamil land, cured the Pāṇṭiya king with the sacred ash and defeated the Jains of Madurai in the fire and water ordeals.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:campantar"], "disputes": ["dsp:tamil-saiva-and-jain-contests"], "notes": "Section-level locator. The account continues with the Jains' impalement, which the tradition narrates; see the dispute record.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:periya-puranam:tirunavukkaracu-nayanar-puranam", "source": "src:periya-puranam", "location": {"ref": "tirunavukkaracu-nayanar-puranam"}, "paraphrase": "Appar left Jainism, was cured of colic by grace, survived the king's lime-kiln, poison, elephant and the sea by singing Śiva's names, and served by clearing grass from temple courtyards; offered gold and jewels by Śiva as a test, he threw them away as potsherds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "practice"], "teachers": ["tch:appar"], "practices": ["prc:saiva-carya"], "disputes": ["dsp:tamil-saiva-and-jain-contests"], "notes": "Section-level locator; the gold episode moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
